            <ArticleTitle>A sneeze: an unusual trigger for aortic dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-200619</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013200619</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a rare case of type B thoracic aortic dissection resulting from a forceful sneeze in a 57-year-old man. The presenting clinical features were not typical and consisted of pleuritic chest pain and breathlessness following a forceful sneeze. There was no haemodynamic compromise. The diagnosis was made incidentally when he underwent a CT pulmonary angiography as part of pulmonary embolism work-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
